#%RAML 1.0 Trait
usage: |
  Apply to any method that should accept a client-supplied correlation id. Response-side
  echoing of X-Correlation-Id is handled globally in each Mule app's error/response
  handling (Step 3+), not modeled per response code here — RAML trait parameters would
  require a fixed responseCode at every call site, which varies per method (200/201/204)
  and adds no contract value over documenting the behavior once, here.
headers:
  X-Correlation-Id:
    description: |
      Client-supplied correlation id. If omitted, the API generates one and returns it
      in the X-Correlation-Id response header on every response, success or error.
    type: string
    required: false
    example: "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890"
